{
  "title": "daily.dev \u2014 Professional networking / Developer tools / Social network (19,856\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: daily.dev\nDomain: Professional networking / Developer tools / Social network | Scale: large | Stars: 19,856\nProblem: daily.dev is a professional network that helps developers stay updated with personalized content, discover knowledge effortlessly, and collaborate with peers. It solves the challenge of information overload and fragmented learning for busy developers.\nTarget users: Software developers, Software engineers, Tech professionals, Developer communities\nCore features: Personalized news feed with developer content; Browser extension (Chrome, Edge, Firefox); Progressive Web App (PWA) for mobile; Developer communities and groups; Developer search engine; Offline functionality; DevCard profile and social sharing\nIntegrations: GitHub (via GitHub Actions for DevCard), Chrome Web Store, Microsoft Edge Add-ons, Firefox Add-ons, Apple Safari (implied)\nTech stack: React (monorepo with extension and webapp) + Node.js with TypeORM + PostgreSQL (inferred from TypeORM migrations) + Docker, Docker Compose\nKey libraries: TypeORM, React, Progressive Web App APIs, Browser Extension APIs\nArchitecture: microservices\nDesign lessons:\n- Complex system architecture with multiple isolated services (extension, webapp, API, authentication, monetization) despite simple user-facing interface\n- Multi-platform delivery strategy using web extension APIs, PWA, and traditional web app to maximize developer reach\n- Monorepo pattern for frontend code sharing between browser extension and web application reduces duplication\n- Community-first approach with open contribution model and GitHub-centric documentation/feedback loops",
